> A reversal request keeps the current direction

The reset head points right with its tail to the left. Requesting left would reverse into the body, so the source ignores it and advances one cell right. Observation planes describe the resulting head, body and food.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/snake_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace e=dm::rl::environments;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");e::Snake env;env.reset(1);auto before=env.head();env.step(3);auto after=env.head();std::vector<double>values{double(before.first),double(before.second),double(after.first),double(after.second)};if(after.first!=before.first||after.second!=before.second+1)return 1;std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");for(size_t i=0;i<values.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,values[i]);dm::nn::save_npz("build/snake_worked.npz",{{"values",dm::nn::from_vector(values)}});std::vector<double>x(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);const double low=std::min(0.,*std::min_element(values.begin(),values.end())),high=std::max(0.,*std::max_element(values.begin(),values.end())),span=std::max(1e-9,high-low);dm::graphics::RPlot::create().ylim(low-.05*span,high+.05*span).bars(x,values,"computed values",{37,99,235}).title("A reversal request keeps the current direction").x_label("Coordinate in displayed calculation").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/snake_worked.svg");}
