> A fixed-action diagnostic trajectory

This additional trace starts from seed1 and repeatedly applies the displayed constant action until the first done flag or200 steps. It shows state evolution and rewards; it is not a learned-policy result. The complete original policy comparison above remains the experiment.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/snake_trajectory.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace e=dm::rl::environments;e::Snake env;auto observation=env.reset(1);std::vector<double>step{0},coordinate{double(env.head().second)},returns{0};for(int t=1;t<=200;++t){auto result=env.step(e::Action(1));step.push_back(t);coordinate.push_back(env.head().second);returns.push_back(returns.back()+result.reward);if(result.done())break;}dm::nn::save_npz("build/snake_trajectory.npz",{{"step",dm::nn::from_vector(step)},{"head_column",dm::nn::from_vector(coordinate)},{"return",dm::nn::from_vector(returns)}});dm::graphics::RPlot::create().lines(step,coordinate,"head column",{37,99,235}).x_label("Environment step").y_label("Head column").title("Snake fixed-action state trace").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/snake_trajectory.svg");std::print("{} transitions; cumulative reward {:.6f}.\n",step.size()-1,returns.back());}
```
